.TH "PERCH-ACCOUNT" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-account \- add, list, password, disable, enable, or delete accounts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch account [OPTIONS] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Manage local mailbox accounts. Creating an account also creates the default mailbox set: INBOX, Sent, Drafts, Trash, Junk, and Archive.
.PP
Deleting an account removes its addresses, mailboxes, and messages. Outbound history is retained with the account reference cleared.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Passwords are hashed with Argon2id.
.IP \(bu 2
Account changes are written to SQLite and apply without restarting serve.
.IP \(bu 2
Account deletion is immediate and cannot be undone. Local message blobs are released; S3 tombstones are left for gc.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
create an account
.TP
.B list
list accounts
.TP
.B passwd
change an account password
.TP
.B disable
disable an account
.TP
.B enable
enable an account
.TP
.B delete
delete an account and all of its messages
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch account add \-\-email you@example.com

perch account list

perch account passwd \-\-email you@example.com

perch account delete \-\-email you@example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-add\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-delete\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-disable\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-enable\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-list\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\-passwd\fR(1)
